 saved states yet", "Turn On Hardcore Mode?", "Achievements are earned as on the original console, with no help. While Hardcore Mode is on, save states and fast-forward are off: every game starts from the beginning and only the game's own saves are kept. RetroArch also blocks cheats, rewind and slow motion. You can turn it off at any time.", "Turn On", "Not available in Hardcore Mode", "Save states are off in Hardcore Mode", "SD1", "System and saves", "{0} free of {1}", "Games card", "No card", "Checking…", "Read-only", "The card has errors: games can be played, nothing can be written to it", "Unreadable", "No supported file system (exFAT, FAT32, ext4)", "Ejected", "SD2 ejected: safe to remove", "Eject SD2", "Use SD2 Again", "Create Game Folders", "Adds a folder for each system. Nothing is deleted.", "Format SD2", "Erases everything on the card", "Press again • everything on SD2 will be erased", "BACKUP TO SD2", "SD2 inserted", "Last backup: {0}", "Never backed up", "Insert an SD2 card to back up", "Backup Content", "All", "{0} of {1}", "SD2 removed", "Restore from SD2", "Replaces the data on SD1 with a backup", "Backup of a previous SD1", "Restore it, or keep it aside and start a new backup", "SD2 is read-only", "Profiles & Settings", "Always included. Passwords and accounts are never copied.", "Saves", "Save States", "Game Library", "Play history and collections", "Screenshots & Recordings", "You can format it in Settings › System › Storage", "Covers & Metadata", "Downloaded game information; it can take a lot of space", "New SD2 card: no games found", "Don't Use", "SD2 can't be read", "Erase everything on SD2 ({0})?", "Format", "Restore \"{0}\"?", "SD2 removed: game saved and closed", "This console", "Backup found on SD2", "Start from Scratch", "Restoring…", "Backing up…", "Backup to SD2", "The backup could not be completed", "Formatting SD2", "Formatting…", "SD2 formatted", "The card could not be formatted", "Creating game folders", "Insert the SD2 card with this game", "Its games come back when you insert it again", "Errors found: open Recovery", "Close the game first", "Not in use", "Use SD2", "nuubOS leaves this card alone until you choose to use it", "PROFILE BACKUP", "Backup", "REPAIR & RESET", "Installing update", "Update Channel", "Stable", "RC", "Nightly", "RC and Nightly get new versions first and may have bugs", "The update could not be installed", "Install it from Settings › System › Software Update", "Check Automatically", "Once a day, when connected to Wi-Fi", "Restoring your console", "Keep the console on: it restarts by itself when it is done", "Try Again", "Dusting off your save files…", "Putting the cartridges back in their cases…", "Reminding your games where you left off…", "Untangling the controller cables…", "Giving the high scores back to their owners…", "Polishing every pixel…", "Blowing into the cartridge, just in case…", "Teaching the console your favourite games again…", "What's New", "Scroll", "Polishing the new version…", "Checking every byte twice…", "Making room for new features…", "Tightening a few screws…", "Teaching old buttons new tricks…", "Charge the battery above 30% to install", "The update service cannot be reached. Try again later", "RESTORE", "Destination", "USB Drive", "Restore from Backup", "Entire Console", "What do you want to restore?", "The whole console or a single profile", "Connect a USB drive to back up", "Lost if SD1 is formatted or replaced", "Backup found", "BACKUP", "Starting…", "Waiting for your devices", "No devices yet", "Add a Device", "Another console, a computer or a phone", "DEVICES", "WHAT TO SYNC", "Wants to sync with you", "Accept", "Ignore", "Sync Away from Home", "Finds your devices over the Internet; your data still goes straight between them", "This Console", "Code {0} • Press to show the full ID", "{0}% synced", "Sync Your Saves", "Syncthing keeps your saves the same on all your devices. They travel straight over your network: no account, no cloud. It is not a backup: a save deleted on one device is deleted on the others too.", "What do you want to sync with?", "Another Console", "Two nuubOS consoles share the same saves", "Computer or Server", "A PC or NAS that stays on: where all your consoles meet", "Android Phone", "With the Syncthing-Fork app", "What to Sync", "Choose what this profile shares. Use the same profile on every device: each profile has its own saves.", "On the Other Console", "Turn it on and connect it to the same Wi-Fi network.", "Choose a profile with the same name.", "Open {0}.", "This console: {0}", "Choose the Other Console", "Pick the code the other console shows. If it found this console first, accept its request.", "Looking for consoles on your network…", "Device {0}", "Confirm on the Other Console", "On the other console, accept the request from {0}. The saves start syncing as soon as both consoles connect.", "Waiting for the other device…", "Install Syncthing on the Computer", "Download Syncthing from syncthing.net (Windows, macOS, Linux) or install the Syncthing app on your NAS.", "Start it: its page opens in the browser.", "Keep it running: it is where all your consoles meet.", "Add This Console", "In Syncthing on the computer choose Add Remote Device and pick this console among the nearby devices (code {0}), or type its ID:", "Waiting for the request from the computer…", "Accept the Folders", "The computer now asks to add the nuubOS folders: accept them and choose where to keep them.", "For more consoles, repeat this guide on each one; on the computer, add them to the folders you already have.", "Install Syncthing-Fork", "On your Android phone install Syncthing-Fork from F-Droid or Google Play and open it.", "Connect the phone to the same Wi-Fi network.", "Scan This Code", "In Syncthing-Fork open Devices, tap + and scan this code. Then accept the request that appears here.", "Waiting for the request from the phone…", "The phone now asks to add the nuubOS folders: accept them and choose where to keep them.", "You're All Set", "{0} is connected. From now on your saves sync by themselves whenever both devices are on.", "Add it on your other device, or scan the code with your phone.", "New sync request", "Cannot sync", "Syncthing is still starting. Try again in a moment.", "Device ID", "Allow Relays", "If a direct connection is impossible, the encrypted data may pass through public Syncthing servers", "Covers & Metadata", "Shared by every profile on this console", "Play Activity", "Time played and Recently Played, added up across your devices", "Saves match when the game file has the same name on every device.", "SYNCTHING", "Continue Watching", "Videos", "Recordings", "Music", "Playlists", "Browse", "Shuffle All", "New Playlist", "Playlist name", "Add to Playlist", "Remove from Playlist", "Delete Playlist", "Rename Playlist", "Removed from the playlist", "Shuffle", "Play from the Beginning", "Resume from {0}", "{0} tracks", "{0} videos", "NOW PLAYING", "UP NEXT", "Music Volume", "Screen Off", "The music keeps playing. Press POWER or START to turn the screen back on.", "Songs", "Unknown Artist", "Put videos in the Videos folder and music in the Music folder: on Internal Storage, SD2, a USB drive or a network location.", "Jellyfin", "Sign in to your Jellyfin server", "Signed in as {0}", "Connect to open it", "This playlist is empty. Add songs from an album with Add to Playlist.", "Episode {0}", "Network Location", "Album", "Folder", "Options", "MUSIC", "Pause", "Next Track", "Previous Track", "Game Volume", "Stop Music", "Places", "Copy to Other Panel", "Move to Other Panel", "{0} selected", "{0} items", "Select All", "Clear Selection", "Sort", "Name", "Size", "Date", "Same Folder in Other Panel", "Calculating…", "Delete {0} items?", "Actions", "Mark", "Copying {0}", "Moving {0}", "Loading…", "Open a folder in the other panel first", "A folder cannot go inside itself", "Modified {0}", "Sort: {0}", "Done: {0}", "Remove Location", "Subtitles", "Play", "