t can make the console unstable. Press again to turn it on.", "1 port", "{0} ports", "Music & Videos Access", "Off: this port cannot see your music and videos", "On: this port can read your music and videos, not change them", "1x", "2x", "Auto: 1x on the console, 2x on a TV", "2x is sharper but can slow the game down", "Fast can draw smoke and glass wrong", "Terminal", "TERMINAL", "Quit Terminal", "The terminal could not be opened", "Press Power to Sleep", "Hold the power button for the power menu.", "The power button opens the power menu.", "RetroArch in the Quick Menu", "Opens RetroArch's own menu during a game", "RetroArch could not be opened", "RETROARCH", "Quit RetroArch", "Reset RetroArch Settings", "Puts the current user's RetroArch options, core options and remaps back to the defaults. Games, saves and states are kept.", "RetroArch settings reset", "Disc", "Disc {0}", "{0} of {1}", "Vibration Intensity", "Light", "Strong", "Skips the faintest vibration some games keep sending", "Every vibration the game asks for", "Vibration", "Picture Position", "Where the game sits when it does not fill the screen", "Top", "Center", "Bottom", "Square Pixels", "Games", "The ROM folder on this console's card, shared by every profile", "Games on SD2", "The SD2 card's ROM folder; it waits while the card is out", "Volume Button Step", "Cover Region", "Box art from this region when there is one. Fill Missing Data changes the covers already downloaded.", "USA", "Europe", "Japan", "World", "Small Screen Position", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left", "Top Right", "Top Left", "Ports on SD2", "PortMaster and the ports in the ports folder of the SD2 card. The ports of the other card stay there.", "Moving ports", "{0} ports were already there: their copies stayed on the other card", "The ports could not be moved", "Data on SD2", "Moving…", "Waiting for the SD2 card", "{0} files were already there: the other copies are in the conflicts folder", "Saves, states, BIOS and covers", "Use SD1 without the card's data?", "Use SD1", "SD2 holds your data: move it to SD1 first", "Insert the SD2 card with your data", "The data could not be moved", "Offline Achievements", "Sent when you are back online", "Casual only: off in Hardcore Mode", "System ({0})", "{0} games use their own settings", "Apply to All Games", "Reset System Settings", "{0} Settings", "Settings shared by every game of this system", "System Settings", "Emulator and picture for all the games of a system", "Controls", "Choose what each button does in the game", "Reset Controls", "Cross", "Circle", "Triangle", "Square", "Custom", "Frameskip", "Auto (up to 3)", "Auto skips frames only when the game slows down", "Wrap Around Rows", "On Home, going past the last item returns to the first", "Search System", "Change it for a port of a game from another system.", "As in Settings ({0})", "Same as the game ({0})", "Advanced Search", "Change it if the game is not found or the match is wrong.", "Permanently deletes the game's folder and everything in it for every user. Saves are kept."];

    in-out property <string> topbar-time: "--:--";
    in-out property <string> current-user-name: root.i18n-strings[204];
    in-out property <image> current-user-avatar;
    in-out property <bool> current-user-avatar-available: false;
    in-out property <string> wifi-state: "disconnected";
    in-out property <int> battery-percent: -1;
    in-out property <string> battery-state: "unknown";
    /* statusd BATTERY_HEALTH (power_supply health, lowercase-dashed). */
    in-out property <string> battery-health: "unknown";
    in-out property <string> battery-label: "--%";
    /* Connected external controllers in player order (Controllers service). */
    in-out property <[TopbarController]> topbar-controllers: [];
    property <int> controller-count: root.topbar-controllers.length;

    in-out property <bool> settings-open: false;

    /* Home (EPIC-001) and Game Library browsing (EPIC-011), fed by
     * nuubos-libraryd. home-row: 0 Recently Played, 1 Systems,
     * 2 Collections (ends with New Collection), 3 Applications; each row
     * remembers its own position. */
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> home-recent: [];
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> home-systems: [];
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> home-collections: [];
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> home-apps: [];
    in-out property <int> home-row: 0;
    in-out property <int> home-recent-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> home-systems-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> home-collections-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> home-apps-index: 0;
    /* Home modal sheet (Add to Collection, Manage): a list of choices,
     * check = -1 none, 0 off, 1 on; armed = waiting for the confirming
     * press (prompt in detail). */
    /* Find a Game (Select on Home, user request 2026-10-10): a Home view,
     * zones 0 search bar, 1 filter chips, 2 results strip, 3 surprise
     * buttons. findui.rs owns the state. */
    in-out property <bool> find-open: false;
    in-out property <int> find-zone: 0;
    in-out property <string> find-query: "";
    in-out property <[FindChip]> find-chips: [];
    in-out property <int> find-chip-index: 0;
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> find-results: [];
    in-out property <int> find-result-index: 0;
    in-out property <string> find-status: "";
    in-out property <int> find-surprise-index: 0;
    in-out property <bool> home-sheet-open: false;
    in-out property <string> home-sheet-title: "";
    in-out property <[HomeSheetItem]> home-sheet-items: [];
    in-out property <int> home-sheet-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> home-sheet-scroll: 0;
    out property <int> home-sheet-visible-rows: max(3, min(7, floor((root.height - 200px) / 52px)));
    /* Start Game (Confirm held on a game card, user request 2026-10-11):
     * a bottom sheet over Home. Row 0 = Start from the Beginning, rows
     * 1.. = start-sheet-items (newest first); start-sheet-scroll is the
     * first save shown. */
    in-out property <bool> start-sheet-open: false;
    in-out property <string> start-sheet-title: "";
    in-out property <string> start-sheet-system: "";
    in-out property <image> start-sheet-cover;
    in-out property <bool> start-sheet-has-cover: false;
    in-out property <[StartSheetItem]> start-sheet-items: [];
    /* RetroAchievements hardcore: no states listed, a note instead. */
    in-out property <bool> start-sheet-hardcore: false;
    in-out property <int> start-sheet-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> start-sheet-scroll: 0;
    out property <int> start-sheet-visible-rows: max(1, min(8, floor((root.height - 286px) / 50px)));
    /* A Home modal (sheet) owns Confirm/Back. */
    property <bool> home-modal: root.home-sheet-open || root.start-sheet-open;
    in-out property <bool> library-scanning: false;
    /* Picks the playful message of empty Home sections (Rust, per session
     * / user switch). */
    in-out property <int> home-empty-variant: 0;
    in-out property <string> home-notice: "";
    in-out property <bool> library-open: false;
    /* Game loading screen (user request 2026-10-09): shown from the launch
     * request until the game session ends; the bar animates only while
     * the game is starting (busy), so Home stops drawing under RetroArch. */
    in property <bool> launch-open: false;
    in property <bool> launch-busy: false;
    in property <string> launch-title;
    in property <string> launch-system;
    in property <color> launch-accent;
    in property <image> launch-cover;
    in property <bool> launch-has-cover: false;
    in-out property <string> library-title: "";
    in-out property <string> library-detail: "";
    in-out property <[HomeCard]> library-games: [];
    in-out property <int> library-index: 0;
    in-out property <float> library-aspect: 0.75;
    /* The shelf tile the page was opened from (kind, icon, colour). */
    in-out property <HomeCard> library-card;
    in-out property <int> context-face-position: -1;
    /* Settings pages: label of an extra action on the north face
     * (e.g. Remove on a Web bookmark); empty = none. */
    in-out property <string> settings-north-hint: "";

    /* Home metrics, derived from the logical window (never a scaled
     * canvas): type and spacing grow mildly with the height, card sizes
     * follow the space actually available. */
    property <float> home-s: max(1.0, min(1.4, root.height / 480px));
    property <length> home-pad: 22px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-top-pad: 8px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-rows-h: root.height - 102px - root.home-top-pad;
    property <length> home-label-h: 40px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-info-h: 84px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-gap: 16px * root.home-s;
    /* The Home scrolls vertically (user request 2026-10-09: bigger
     * content, more spacing, readable text). Recently Played covers take
     * about half the height; the two shelves together with the info panel
     * of the covers fill one screen, so with a shelf selected the column
     * ends exactly at the bottom: no empty space under Applications. */
    property <length> home-section-gap: 14px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-bottom-pad: 14px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-big-h: max(130px, min(root.home-rows-h * 0.52,
        root.home-rows-h - root.home-label-h - root.home-info-h - 24px * root.home-s));
    property <length> home-chip-h: max(64px * root.home-s, min(96px * root.home-s,
        (root.home-rows-h - root.home-info-h - 2 * root.home-label-h - root.home-section-gap
         - root.home-bottom-pad) / 2));
    property <length> home-chip-w: max(200px * root.home-s, min(300px * root.home-s,
        (root.width - 2 * root.home-pad) / 2.3));
    /* Systems and Collections showcase cards: the games inside take most
     * of the card (user request 2026-10-10). */
    property <length> home-show-h: max(110px, min(root.home-rows-h * 0.42, 260px * root.home-s));
    property <length> home-show-w: min(root.home-show-h * 1.75, (root.width - 2 * root.home-pad) * 0.86);
    property <length> home-y1: root.home-label-h + root.home-big-h + root.home-info-h + root.home-section-gap;
    property <length> home-y2: root.home-y1 + root.home-label-h + root.home-show-h + root.home-section-gap;
    property <length> home-y3: root.home-y2 + root.home-label-h + root.home-show-h + root.home-section-gap;
    property <length> home-total-h: root.home-y3 + root.home-label-h + root.home-chip-h + root.home-bottom-pad;
    property <length> home-max-scroll: max(0px, root.home-total-h - root.home-rows-h);
    /* A section stops one edge fade below the top, so the fade never
     * dims its title (it covers the end of the section above). */
    property <length> home-fade-h: 20px * root.home-s;
    property <length> home-v-scroll: root.home-row == 0 ? 0px
        : max(0px, min((root.home-row == 1 ? root.home-y1 : root.home-row == 2 ? root.home-y2 : root.home-y3)
            - root.home-fade-h, root.home-max-scroll));
    /* System / collection page: a header with the platform's identity. */
    /* Compact header; the info panel (title and chips on two lines like
     * the Home) opens right under the focused row, the rows below move
     * down by library-info-h (user request 2026-10-10). */
    property <length> library-head-h: 42px * root.home-s;
    property <length> library-info-h: 78px * root.home-s;
    property <length> library-view-h: root.home-rows-h - root.library-head-h;
    /* Grid density: about one column per 320 logical px (2 on handhelds,
     * up to 5 on wide screens); a cover uses up to 82 % of the height
     * left by the info panel, so the next row peeks in. */
    property <int> library-target-columns: max(2, min(5, round(root.width / 320px)));
    property <length> library-cell-h: max(110px, min((root.library-view-h - root.library-info-h) * 0.82,
        ((root.width - 2 * root.home-pad + root.home-gap) / root.library-target-columns - root.home-gap)
        / root.library-aspect));
    property <length> library-cell-w: root.library-cell-h * root.library-aspect;
    /* +0.01: when the width sets the cell (square screens) the quotient is
     * the column count itself and float error would floor it one lower. */
    out property <int> library-columns: max(1, floor((root.width - 2 * root.home-pad + root.home-gap)
        / (root.library-cell-w + root.home-gap) + 0.01));
    /* Rust decodes covers once at this logical height (x scale factor)
     * and only for grid rows near the visible ones. */
    out property <length> home-cover-h: max(root.home-big-h, root.library-cell-h);
    out property <int> library-visible-rows: max(1, ceil(root.library-view-h
        / (root.library-cell-h + root.home-gap)));
    property <HomeCard> home-focused: root.library-open ? root.library-games[root.library-index]
        : root.find-open ? root.find-results[root.find-result-index]
        : root.home-row == 0 ? root.home-recent[root.home-recent-index]
        : root.home-row == 1 ? root.home-systems[root.home-systems-index]
        : root.home-row == 2 ? root.home-collections[root.home-collections-index]
        : root.home-apps[root.home-apps-index];
    property <bool> home-focus-valid: root.library-open ? root.library-games.length > 0
        : root.find-open ? root.find-zone == 2 && root.find-results.length > 0
        : root.home-row == 0 ? root.home-recent.length > 0
        : root.home-row == 1 ? root.home-systems.length > 0
        : root.home-row == 2 ? root.home-collections.length > 0
        : root.home-apps.length > 0;
    in-out property <int> settings-selected-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> general-index: 0;
    in-out property <int> general-scroll-offset: 0;
